# AGENTS.local.md — local deploy notes (not tracked)

Copy this file to `AGENTS.local.md` (already covered by `.gitignore` — verify
it's actually listed there, this template ships no `.gitignore` of its own)
and fill it in with the real, machine-specific details of wherever *you*
deploy this project. `AGENTS.md` should stay generic and portable so it's
useful to anyone who forks or reuses this project on their own
infrastructure; this file is where the specifics of one particular
deployment actually live.

Typical contents:

## Deploy target

Host, IP/hostname, how you reach it (SSH key, Tailscale, etc.), OS/arch
constraints that shape the build (e.g. a low-RAM board that can't build its
own frontend).

## Co-located services

If this deploys alongside something else on shared hardware, name it and
note anything that must not be disrupted. (Example: a home-automation
system, a media server, another app on the same box — whatever it actually
is for you. There is nothing generic about this section; it only exists
because *your* target isn't a blank machine.)

## Hard rules specific to this deployment

Anything that would be wrong advice for someone deploying elsewhere but is
load-bearing for this one target — port choices made to avoid a collision,
"never build on-device", that kind of thing.

## Runbook

The actual build/transfer/run/verify commands, with real hostnames and
paths. `AGENTS.md` should describe the *shape* of the deploy process
generically; this is where the literal, copy-pasteable version lives.

## Gotchas and incident history

Deployment-specific lessons learned the hard way — hardware quirks, past
outages on this specific box, anything future-you or a future agent
shouldn't have to rediscover.
